Sigh. This evening I began a chaotic male Elven wizard, expecting the
usual instadeath or death from inherent weakness. But surprisingly, a
LOT of good things happened.

First, on dlvl 2 I found two altars, one coaligned and one lawful. This
didn't help me straightaway - more on this later.

Then, I got to Minetown and lo and behold, pmcalpin(who, by the way,
just ascended - bravo!) left a bones with Magicbane, +1 gauntlets of
dexterity, and a nice collection of scrolls. Got skilled in dagger, and
went down some more.

I found _three bones piles_ on one level - two monks and a wizard. This
obviously led to a lot of spell learning (after BUCing each spellbook
on the dlvl2 altars) - but unfortunately not Magic Missile. I also got a
lot of holy water and did some blessing. Used my initial magic marker to
write blessed identifies.

Got my bag of holding in Sokoban. 'nuff said...

Then, I found some blessed speed boots on a nymph. I started writing
scrolls and ended up with an AC of about -13. Paid off some of the
priests and it got to -22. Smooth sailing. I tried out Medusa but I
figured that I needed some reflection first as the titan casting spells
all over the map scared me.

I went back up and noticed this guy with a cool scroll shop. I had just
made myself invisible, though, and this cockatrice comes walking by (you
can see it coming already... :)) so I killed it, stoned the shopkeep. I
still had ESP! Yay for being chaotic (?) Anyway, then a NURSE comes
along... 

"Hmm, maybe I should dance."

I take off my stuff and I gain about 10 hit points. She teleports into
the shop and I follow her.

Guess where I left the cockatrice corpse?

